{# Renders the server's tool catalog into an agent-facing tool-calling format.
   Used for hosts/prompts that need prompt-level tool definitions (Hermes/LLaMA style).
   Context: tools = [ToolSpec], workspace_root = str -#}
You have access to the following tools, served by Protocol-X Tool MCP (sandboxed, workspace root: {{ workspace_root }}).
To call a tool, emit a JSON object inside <tool_call>...</tool_call> tags.

<tools>
{% for tool in tools -%}
{
  "name": "{{ tool.name }}",
  "description": "{{ tool.description }}",
  "parameters": {{ tool.input_schema | tojson(indent=2) }}
}{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}
{% endfor -%}
</tools>

Call format:
<tool_call>
{"name": "<tool_name>", "arguments": {<arg_dict>}}
</tool_call>

Rules (enforced server-side, violations return structured errors):
- arguments must validate against the tool's JSON Schema (additionalProperties: false).
- file paths are workspace-relative; "../" escapes are rejected.
- results >1 MB are persisted to the workspace and returned as resource links.
- binary results arrive as base64 content blocks with an explicit mime type.
